/* book: the chapter, paragraph by paragraph (first sentences):
   - The cost of finding a fault rises at each level; a common rule of thumb is about ten times per level.
   - C = (N × cw + Np × cp) ÷ Ng
   - where C is the wafer-sort plus packaging cost per good die shipped (₹), N the die on the wafer, cw the wafer-sort cost per die, Np the die that reach packaging, cp the packaging cost per die and Ng the good die shipped.
   - An SoC is assembled from cores: processor, memory controller, USB, DSP, analog blocks, often from different vendors.
   - where T is a core's test time in clocks, P its number of patterns and ℓ the length of its longest wrapper scan chain.
   - In-circuit test (ICT) presses a bed of nails onto the board's nets and measures each part: fast, but the fixture is costly and fits one board.
   - Test coding, as some syllabi call it, is how a test is written down for the tester and kept small.
*/
