/* book exam traps: Dividing by all die instead of good die shipped. Cost per good die uses the good parts that leave the line. | Thinking wafer sort replaces final test. Bonding faults and speed failures appear only after assembly. | Mixing up scan (chip-internal DFT) and boundary scan (pins and board wiring). They use different cells and catch different faults. | Assuming a wider TAM always speeds a core. A core with fixed internal chains cannot use more wires than it has chains. | Testing every core at once without checking power. Scan switching in all cores together can exceed the package's power limit. */
